  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ARCH - Action for Regional Climate Help: Bottom-Up Youth Climate Governance in North-East Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Civil society in Egypt and Sudan, especially the youth, is hardly involved in political discourse and processes in the areas of reducing CO2 emissions and adapting to climate change. Before the project began, this was due, among others, to the fragmentation of the youth movement as well as a lack of technical skills and contacts with both the authorities and potential partner and donor institutions. The aim of the project was to strengthen the resources, the network, and the voice of Sudanese and Egyptian youth organisations (YLOs). YLOs should be able to engage more effectively in the fight for climate protection and adaptation to climate change. To this end, the project focused on experience-based learning, simulation games and futurology. The aim is for the YLOs to use their newly acquired skills to draft high-quality policy proposals, develop climate initiatives, and enter dialogue with national policymakers.</narrative>
  </description>
